IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition (SSO informal consolidation, version in force 6/5/2026 to 20/10/2026):
-- Part 4 Division 8, ss 139, 140 and 141: documents made out of Singapore, charges created before 29 December 1967,
-- and the application of the Division to a foreign company. Layer 1: the law, objectively.
-- This module is imported by sgk-div8-registration.l4 (ss 131 to 133 take the s 139 extension from here).
-- A date is written Date day month year; a period is counted only by sg-periods.l4.
-- Marks used in the comments: "FALSE-kind" and "NOTHING-kind" say why a branch answers JUST FALSE or NOTHING;
-- "fork F-Kn" points at the fork register of NOTES.md.

§ `Section 139: documents made out of Singapore`

-- src:11466 | 139. Where under this Division an instrument, deed, statement or
-- src:11467 | other document is required to be lodged with the Registrar within a
-- src:11468 | specified time, the time so specified is, by force of this section, in
-- src:11473 | relation to an instrument, deed, statement or other document executed
-- src:11474 | or made in a place out of Singapore, extended by 7 days or such
-- src:11475 | further periods as the Registrar may from time to time allow.
@ref s 139 (src:11466-11475)
GIVEN `the document was executed or made in a place out of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of further days the Registrar has allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 139 the number of days added to the time specified` MEANS
    IF `the document was executed or made in a place out of Singapore`
    THEN 7 PLUS `the number of further days the Registrar has allowed`   -- fork F-K1: "7 days or such further periods" read as 7 days plus any further days allowed
    ELSE 0                                                               -- no extension for a document made in Singapore (the arithmetic helper; s 139 itself says nothing of one, see the next function)

@ref s 139 (src:11466-11475)
GIVEN `the document is required under Division 8 of Part 4 to be lodged with the Registrar within a specified time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document was executed or made in a place out of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of further days the Registrar has allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 139 the time specified is extended by` MEANS
    IF `the document is required under Division 8 of Part 4 to be lodged with the Registrar within a specified time` AND `the document was executed or made in a place out of Singapore`
    THEN JUST (`s 139 the number of days added to the time specified` `the document was executed or made in a place out of Singapore` `the number of further days the Registrar has allowed`)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in relation to an instrument, deed, statement or other document executed or made in a place out of Singapore" names the documents whose time is extended; it says nothing of a document made in Singapore

-- "the time so specified is ... extended": the last day on which a document may be lodged where this Division specifies N days after an event.
@ref s 139 (src:11466-11475)
GIVEN `the day of the event` IS A DATE
      `the number of days this Division specifies` IS A NUMBER
      `the document was executed or made in a place out of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of further days the Registrar has allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`s 139 the last day for lodging the document` MEANS
    `period: the last day of a period after` `the day of the event`
        (`the number of days this Division specifies` PLUS `s 139 the number of days added to the time specified` `the document was executed or made in a place out of Singapore` `the number of further days the Registrar has allowed`)
        Days

§ `Section 140: charges created before 29 December 1967`

-- src:11479 | 140. Except as is otherwise expressly provided, this Division
-- src:11480 | applies to any charge that on 29 December 1967 was registrable under
-- src:11481 | any of the repealed written laws but which at that date was not
-- src:11482 | registered under any of those laws.
@ref s 140 (src:11479-11482)
GIVEN `on 29 December 1967 the charge was registrable under one of the repealed written laws` IS A BOOLEAN
      `on 29 December 1967 the charge was not registered under any of those laws` IS A BOOLEAN
      `this Division expressly provides otherwise for the charge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 140 this Division applies to the charge` MEANS
    IF `this Division expressly provides otherwise for the charge`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Except as is otherwise expressly provided, this Division applies to any charge ..." (an "except" met: fork F-K2)
    ELSE (IF `on 29 December 1967 the charge was registrable under one of the repealed written laws` AND `on 29 December 1967 the charge was not registered under any of those laws`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): section 140 says the Division applies to a charge registrable and unregistered on 29 December 1967; it does not say it applies to no other charge (section 131(3) governs later charges)

§ `Section 141: the Division and a foreign company`

-- src:11486 | 141. A reference in this Division to a company includes a reference
-- src:11487 | to a foreign company if, and only if, it is registered under Division 2
-- src:11488 | of Part 11, but nothing in this Division applies to a charge on property
-- src:11489 | outside Singapore of such foreign company.
@ref s 141 (src:11486-11489)
GIVEN `the foreign company is registered under Division 2 of Part 11` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 141 a reference in Division 8 to a company includes the foreign company` MEANS
    IF `the foreign company is registered under Division 2 of Part 11`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A reference in this Division to a company includes a reference to a foreign company if, and only if, it is registered under Division 2 of Part 11"

@ref s 141 (src:11486-11489)
GIVEN `the foreign company is registered under Division 2 of Part 11` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the charge is on property outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 141 this Division applies to the charge of the foreign company` MEANS
    IF `the foreign company is registered under Division 2 of Part 11` AND `the charge is on property outside Singapore`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "nothing in this Division applies to a charge on property outside Singapore of such foreign company"
    ELSE NOTHING      -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the proviso removes only a charge on property outside Singapore of a foreign company registered under Division 2 of Part 11; for any other charge of such a company it is silent (the first limb of the section makes the reference to a company include the foreign company)
